From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1ma <hello@1ma.ai>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:10:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] 1ma: resume idle Codex sessions after a CLI update

bb keeps one codex app-server process per thread. When Homebrew or npm
updates Codex, that process keeps running from the old installation; on
macOS Homebrew deletes the old version's folder, so the next turn's Code Mode
asks the old process for files that are gone. Before a turn, when no Codex
turn or compaction is open, the bridge now checks whether the launched
executable was replaced (device, inode, modification time and size of the file the
command resolves to) and, if so, restores the same thread in a new process
with thread/resume, keeping the thread id, history, CODEX_HOME and the
account pool connection. A running turn is never interrupted and never
retried. Both ways an update replaces Codex are covered: Homebrew points the
command at a new versioned file, npm writes a new file at the same path (seen
on Linux with @openai/codex 0.168.0 -> 0.169.0: same path and size, new
inode and mtime). A rebuild whose turn carries no env vars keeps the
session's own, which bb's signature check already treats as unchanged.
